{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling","id":806874,"title":"Turning a Vampire into a Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T03:20:04-08:00","id":806874,"title":"Turning a Vampire into a Changeling","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> so, in our last session of my CtL (1st ed) game something rather unpleasant happened to one of the characters. After being caught by a vampire, i rolled a percentile die to see if there would be any chance of him being sired and alas, i rolled a 99 (on a scale of 00 to 99). So, formerly a darkling, he's now a mekhet at blood potency 1 which doesn't really come in too handy when considering that most of our chronicle takes place when the sun is up.<br /> <br /> Here's the deal: I want to create an opportunity to turn the character back into either a changeling or a mere mortal, but I am lacking great ideas. Currently, my thought process was like this: A vampire is essentially the corpse of a human animated by Vitae, so killing a vampire would turn him into a mere corpse and make reanimation as a human possible. Only problem is that, as far as I am aware, all vampires turn into ashes once they die, thus leaving no corpse to be reanimated.<br /> <br /> Actually reanimating a corpse is another problem. Sin-Eaters are capable of doing so, but the group (as in, the characters) doesn't even know they exist and I don't wanna throw in another game line into what is currently a Changeling game with heavy VtR crossover elements. Mummy is coming to the chronicle soon as I have prepared a story arc using one of the Cursed as an antagonist.<br /> <br /> To make pondering this subject a little easier: The group consists of four characters, two of which are at wyrd 1 and one at wyrd 2 (plus a vampire, obviously). I personally treat changelings as humans who have their soul mutated by the influence of the gentry, turning them into changelings. So their bodies are actually mortal bodies plus a few positives that come from being able to use glamour, contracts, etc.<br /> <br /> If you have some ideas about the topic at hand, please help me out, guys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:16:35-08:00","id":806892,"title":"","content":"Well, technically speaking, the embrace wouldn't have worked in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:26:40-08:00","id":806894,"title":"","content":"Maybe he become Blood Addicted and he <i>thinks</i> he is now vampire - but mechanically he still is Darkling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:46:30-08:00","id":806912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling#post806874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally treat changelings as humans who have their soul mutated by the influence of the gentry, turning them into changelings. So their bodies are actually mortal bodies plus a few positives that come from being able to use glamour, contracts, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The advantage here is that you can rule that mutation is still present, just overtaken by the Blood - ie, turning him back into a human will automatically turn him back into a changeling.<br /> <br /> Something from a goblin market that restores life to the dead... you could rule that it's powerful enough to overcome the vampiric nature and restore someone to human (and thus him to changeling). But they owe some hobgoblin big for it - or if they've paid the hob already, they owe someone else big for whatever it was - or if they stole it, that's still hanging over their heads.<br /> <br /> If the sun is the main logistical problem for the campaign, maybe a market will also have something that protects against it (the Sun agrees not to burn this vampire so long as he converts to the worship of a Sun god, and encourages one person a day to do the same). Or agrees not to the burn him on any day where he interacts with changelings but no vampires the previous night (essentially, if he acts like a changeling, the Sun promises to treat him like one). Or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:47:54-08:00","id":806913,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts that I believe are within your guidelines:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Gentry probably know the secrets of undoing such changes. Of course, that's not exactly the best option...<br /> <br /> \u2022In the Goblin Market lies a watch that is always two hours behind, and whose hands are made from the purest crystalized regret. Set it back to when an event occurred, speak what happened, and shatter it, and you may undo the consequences of that act. But you're going to have to pay the price...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T05:25:22-08:00","id":806925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling?p=806892#post806892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, technically speaking, the embrace wouldn't have worked in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. That's why I mentioned how I rule Changelings, right?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"321\" data-vbnamecard=\"321\">SunlessNick</a> Yeah, that might be a good option of allowing him to be a changeling instead of a human. I'll have to clear with the player what he prefers. I don't want to force him into being a changeling if he actually enjoys the idea of turning human again. Or being a vampire, for that matter.<br /> <br /> In terms of an item that protects from the sun, I usually don't like bringing this in because it clears the vampire of one of their main weaknesses. I'll think about it still. The Sun contracting a vampire in similar ways to a changeling sounds interesting. However, some bane should still come from it, even if it is only being tired by daylight.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3514\" data-vbnamecard=\"3514\">ZealousChristian24</a> I like the idea with the watch. But sadly, the group managed to destroy the only goblin market in town, so they might have to do some travelling out of Berlin (setting of our chronicle) to find one. It does however also allow the group to make more impactful corrections. For example, our first storyline was one of ritual murder going on in the freehold and the group only slowly finding out who was behind it - and then being betrayed by a person they trusted deeply. If they could undo the first murder, they would render a lot of the things that happened afterwards useless.<br /> <br /> Interactions with the gentry are interesting but probably also quite deadly if we consider how weak these characters actually are in the grand scheme of things. Plus the character in question, now turned vampire, has a tendency of failing with the best of dice pools ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:50:37-08:00","id":806975,"title":"","content":"Other ideas for un-turning the vampling (or compensating for sun-destruction):<br /> <br /> -Create some kind of ritual, such as draining the changepire of all blood, then replacing it with blood from his motley-mates, and have the PCs find out about it. This could bring the victim back to life, but at the price of being tied to the life of the motley: if the motley disbands or a member dies, the victim dies, too. (Maybe it only works if you're tied to the Wyrd and can pledge to a motley, which is why other vamps haven't pulled it off.)<br /> -Encourage the player to take Goblin Vow, either with the sun (&quot;If you promise to hurt me less when I go out, I'll build a bonfire every night this week&quot;) or with something opposed to the sun, like shadows (&quot;If you shield me from the sun, I'll knock out every streetlight in the city&quot;). Have the player use the vow when they need to be day-side, and shift the setting slightly so being day-side is less common.<br /> -Lessen sun penalties in-universe, either for all vampires, or just this one. Can the character be shielded by blankets/protective gear? Is their damage rate one lower, due to the Wyrd's influence?<br /> -Have the player join up with Ordo Dracul. They've got some tricks to mitigate the sun, right?<br /> -Is there a Spring courtier in the party? If the vampling gets injured for being in the sun, can he heal himself with blood from his motley, then have the Spring courtier heal the damage caused by feeding? (This one is a little munchin-y, I admit.)<br /> <br /> Side note: If the player sticks with being a vampire, and is a Mekhet, but still Wyrd-touched, would he start to manifest the Alucinor (dream-pire) bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T08:06:01-08:00","id":807022,"title":"","content":"Ordo was my first thought. The freehold he pledged loyalty to houses a former Ordo member who was exiled for scientific interest in the strix which was close to being a terrible danger for all Kindred in the city. Why would Changelings take up with an exiled vampire? Well, there's something about said vampire and the queen of the autumn court, although not as you might imagine. They simply share a passion or two.<br /> Problem with the Ordo is: There only is this one vampire in the city who has any ties to the Ordo as there was a recent &quot;war&quot; between Ordo and Invictus which the Invictus easily won, taking total control over the cities Kindred society. To clarify this in numbers: Invictus: &gt;100 members. All other covenants combined: &lt;20. (except for VII maybe, I have my plans for my favorite covenant)<br /> <br /> Lessening sun penalties seems ... off, considering that the chronicle focuses a lot on vampires as antagonists. This would make it harder for the group to operate during the day to avoid those pointy-fanged beasts.<br /> <br /> I do like the ritual idea. It would make for an interesting interaction if one of the motley died and they would actually loose half their party due to the former vampire dying as well.<br /> <br /> Yes, I assume the Alucinor bloodline would be a logical step. I haven't thought about it too much because the vampirism only occured last sunday, so I am still planning how a change-pire would actually work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T08:25:01-08:00","id":807032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">i rolled a 99 (on a scale of 00 to 99).</div> </div> </div> </div>This reading posts with this type of whimsy makes me nostalgic. I would point out the storyteller system doesn't use d10 as percentile die, but I'd be penalized by the cosmic Storyteller with a Banality point from <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i>, and confirm my status as a Grump compared to all you Wilders and Childlings. Those were the days, I tell ya'. *waves cane to punctuate point*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-12-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:18:46-08:00","id":807072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling?p=807022#post807022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lessening sun penalties seems ... off, considering that the chronicle focuses a lot on vampires as antagonists. This would make it harder for the group to operate during the day to avoid those pointy-fanged beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if the Sun demands he not interact with vampires in order to earn his reduced or removed burns, that means fighting them will require a bit of finesse: after all, fighting vampires is a very vampire thing to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:03:34-08:00","id":807191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling?p=807032#post807032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This reading posts with this type of whimsy makes me nostalgic. I would point out the storyteller system doesn't use d10 as percentile die, but I'd be penalized by the cosmic Storyteller with a Banality point from <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i>, and confirm my status as a Grump compared to all you Wilders and Childlings. Those were the days, I tell ya'. *waves cane to punctuate point*</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it, I am afraid. I just use percentile dice for whenever something is really unlikely to happen and I don't wanna make it &quot;at least 3 successes out of a 1-die pool.&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"321\" data-vbnamecard=\"321\">SunlessNick</a> Yes, true. But what AceOfAlmonds suggested seemed to me as if it was a little too much. But yes, it would require finesse. And it would make my job a lot easier because a lot of the time I actually don't want them to fight the vampires but outsmart them. Because most vampires tend to be a little too strong for the characters. I'll think about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I'll keep you guys updated to see how it turns out if he actually tries solving the vampirism problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","user":"Dragotarify","date":". 01-12-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:47:31-08:00","id":807222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just use percentile dice for whenever something is really unlikely to happen and I don't wanna make it &quot;at least 3 successes out of a 1-die pool.&quot; or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an incredibly whimsical way to decide in favor of world shattering alterations to core mechanics of the game. It specifically reminds me of when I was a much younger gamer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it, I am afraid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am referencing <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/ChangelingTheDreaming\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling the Dreaming</a>, a role playing game by white wolf publishing, the creators of the world of darkness. It was a game of modern day urban fantasy, where the main characters were reborn fae souls in human bodies, the primary game resource was Glamour which was powered by imagination and creativity and the most deadly bane was Banality, which is humbuggery, boredom and basically the death of the creative soul. The character's interacted in a world of fantasy an imaginary creature that overlaps the mundane world and can be interpreted by mundane witnesses as a bunch of normal people playing pretend. In that sense it was very meta.<br /> <br /> Character age being a vital element to how creative and imaginative a character is it was an important stat, separated in into three categories childings for children, wilders for adolescents and young adult, and grumps for those past youth into later maturity, middle age and ultimately decrepitude.<br /> <br /> I was using those game references to humorously remark how young the game crowd seems and reminds me how old I am, using a reference probably too old for you be familiar with. ie i was poking fun at myself while admiring how carefree and creative you seem beyond the bounds of rules or &quot;more serious role play&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T01:27:33-08:00","id":807707,"title":"","content":"Oh, don't get me wrong, I do know (at least, a little) about Changeling the Dreaming, although I never played it. But thanks for clearing up the details, interesting to know how different these games were. And who knows, maybe I'll get the chance to try classic world of darkness at some point.<br /> <br /> In terms of percentile dice deciding whether something unlikely happens or not, even though I do understand the notion of this being something whimsical, I feel like it something that absolutely fits Changelings mood. I probably wouldn't have went with it this way if it was a Vampire the Requiem chronicle, because vampires, to me, are very calculating and cold in their approach. So whimsical &quot;I am going to role a die for this&quot;-decisions wouldn't fit. To me, it's always about how the way I determine things fit into how the game should feel. For changeling, I want chance and randomness to be a huge factor. For vampire, I would not.<br /> <br /> To return to the topic at hand and maybe expand it a little to &quot;Can a changeling be turned into a Vampire in the first place&quot;: I made this decision in advance when I was determining the structures of vampiric and changeling society in our setting. I knew that the characters would at some point have direct contact with the Kindred and thus, I wanted the vampires to feel like, well, vampires. And one of the most vampiric things to do, besides burning in sunlight and all that good stuff, is to bite someone and turn said person into a vampire.<br /> So, to make it short. I didn't determine whether or not a changeling could be embraced by rolling dice. I just determined wether or not the vampire in question had any interest in embracing the character because I was actually improvising the whole session.<br /> <br /> Anyways, as it turns out, the player of the now-vampire has made up his mind that his character wants to experience being a vampire at least for a while before makin up his mind. Thing is, this won't make it easier for him to undo the whole thing if he doesn't like being a vampire. But oh well, he doesn't know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:43:09-08:00","id":811443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling#post806874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the deal: I want to create an opportunity to turn the character back into either a changeling or a mere mortal, but I am lacking great ideas. Currently, my thought process was like this: A vampire is essentially the corpse of a human animated by Vitae, so killing a vampire would turn him into a mere corpse and make reanimation as a human possible. Only problem is that, as far as I am aware, all vampires turn into ashes once they die, thus leaving no corpse to be reanimated.</div> </div> </div> </div>In second edition vamps don't turn to ash. What happens is when they &quot;die&quot; the body of a vamp reverts to the state decay they should be at. So for a 100 year old vamp that may mean dust. Someone just turned to a vamp won't break down that quickly.<br /> <br /> Personally I take a page from Vampire :the Lost, an exercise some of us did building vamps with changeling rules. Only the darkling isn't a vamp just a blood addicted changeling who thinks he is a vamp. Maybe give leechfinger out of this.<br /> <br /> PS 2nd edition has some different mechanics for daylight damage that could be tweaked to let the vamp walk in daylight. The original spoiled rules prerelease was a lot more lenient. Also covering completely raises them up one level of humanity for sunlight damage.<br /> Also if your mekhet could pick up the nos merit True Wyrm he can stay up as long he is underground 20 or 30 feet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 01-18-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:32:03-08:00","id":811474,"title":"","content":"Normally speaking a changeling can't be Embraced, however that allows for some interesting ideas you could do here. Perhaps the Gentry who originally stole this Changeling, signed some sort of pact or contract with a creature of blood and death. They offered one of their servants would belong to the Undead to fulfill some ancient debt they owed this creature.<b><br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i></b><i> Oh, if you have access to 2nd Edition V:TR I just had a cooler thought. Make it so that the Gentry signed the original deal with one of the Stryx.</i><br /> <br /> After the embrace the character has his mind free of the grip of the Wyld and so starts to remember events that the Gentry commanded him to forget. He remembers his Keeper taking him back to Earth to meet with this dark creature during the early days of his captivity and forcing him to sign a contract in his own blood. A contract that guaranteed it would be his destiny to become a Vampire.<br /> <br /> If he finds that contract and steals it back, it will enable him to undo the deal and return back from the Undead, but only one of the Gentry knows enough about the magic of the contract to do it for him. This gives the character the chance to become a changeling again, but this time by dealing with the Gentry on his own terms. Can he beat the faeries in a bargain though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":". 01-18-2016, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:26:28-08:00","id":817738,"title":"","content":"So how how did you decide to handle it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T03:22:44-08:00","id":822239,"title":"","content":"We've only had two 1v1 sessions since the incident. Right now, he is simply vampiric, trying to work out how to continue his &quot;life&quot;. However, I plan on giving him access to a custom-made bloodline at some point which I am still working on. So nothing concrete yet. The bloodline will probably be somewhat hedge-related, to make the vampire able to walk the hedge and maybe benefit from some of the more changeling-y things in the CofD. Gladly, I have some time because we won't be having a full session before march (exams *sigh*).<br /> <br /> It's been going fine, though. The only problem I can think of is playing as a full group again once all the players are finished with exams in university. One of the changeling characters has recently developed a little bit of phobia against vampires (because one of has been messing with her family while she was in Arcadia). So I will probably have to find a way to make them work together again and not kill each other on sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:54:37-08:00","id":825453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragotarify</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling?p=822239#post822239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've only had two 1v1 sessions since the incident. Right now, he is simply vampiric, trying to work out how to continue his &quot;life&quot;. However, I plan on giving him access to a custom-made bloodline at some point which I am still working on. So nothing concrete yet. The bloodline will probably be somewhat hedge-related, to make the vampire able to walk the hedge and maybe benefit from some of the more changeling-y things in the CofD. Gladly, I have some time because we won't be having a full session before march (exams *sigh*).<br /> <br /> It's been going fine, though. The only problem I can think of is playing as a full group again once all the players are finished with exams in university. One of the changeling characters has recently developed a little bit of phobia against vampires (because one of has been messing with her family while she was in Arcadia). So I will probably have to find a way to make them work together again and not kill each other on sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might check out Children of the Thorns from Danse macabre. <br /> Found this second edition adaption .. Have not vetted yet myself.<br /> <a href=\"http://requiemforkingsmouth.wikia.com/wiki/The_Children_of_the_Thorns\" target=\"_blank\">http://requiemforkingsmouth.wikia.co..._of_the_Thorns</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:21:14-08:00","id":825930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/806874-turning-a-vampire-into-a-changeling?p=825453#post825453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might check out Children of the Thorns from Danse macabre.<br /> Found this second edition adaption .. Have not vetted yet myself.<br /> <a href=\"http://requiemforkingsmouth.wikia.com/wiki/The_Children_of_the_Thorns\" target=\"_blank\">http://requiemforkingsmouth.wikia.co..._of_the_Thorns</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, thanks! I'll see if I can make it work for the character and talk to the player. In the mean time, I have now successfully gotten the rest of the party involved in a conflict with the local Invictus. So, there should be a lot of nightly action for some time, allowing the party to work together. As long as they actually want to, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:55:45-08:00","id":827070,"title":"","content":"There are some bloodlines from the Homebrew posts. I wrote(adapted) one of them, actually, the Kiasyd(Mekhets with Fae blood in their veins).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}